# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fraktal — root .gitignore (centralized)
#
# One authoritative ignore file for the whole repo (O9: single source of truth).
# Sub-directories keep only rules truly local to a generated toolchain (e.g.
# Flutter's own template ignores under HMI/windows/). Everything a human
# authored — Specification/, AGENTS.md, PLC + HMI source, scaffold/,
# pubspec.lock — is TRACKED and must NOT be listed here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
# JetBrains / Android Studio / IntelliJ (per-developer IDE state)
.idea/
*.iml

# --- Agent / assistant local state (not part of the standard) ---
.claude/
.agents/

# --- Dart/Flutter local app data (analysis cache + telemetry; machine-local) ---
.dart_localappdata/

# --- HMI: Flutter build + tool caches (regenerated by pub get / build) ---
# Every package/sub-package has its own .dart_tool (app, gateway, packages/*),
# so match at any depth rather than only at the HMI root.
FraktalCore/HMI/**/.dart_tool/
FraktalCore/HMI/build/
FraktalCore/HMI/.flutter-plugins
FraktalCore/HMI/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
# Flutter's generated Windows glue: ephemeral/ is regenerated by `flutter build`
# and contains machine-local absolute paths + plugin symlinks.
FraktalCore/HMI/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
FraktalCore/HMI/windows/flutter/generated_plugin*
FraktalCore/HMI/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
FraktalCore/HMI/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
# Native OPC UA C build trees (CMake/MSBuild output; the C sources are tracked)
FraktalCore/HMI/native/opcua/**/build/
# Compiled native transports: build outputs copied next to the exes for dev runs.
# The C/C++ sources and CMakeLists ARE tracked; the binaries are not.
*.dll
*.exp
*.ilk
*.pdb
# NOTE: pubspec.lock IS tracked — the HMI is a deployable app and pins versions.

# --- Vendored third-party source (O9 G5: ONE representation per dependency) ---
# mbedtls ships as the upstream release tarball, which the OPC UA native build
# extracts. The extracted tree is therefore build output, not source: tracking
# both put the same dependency in the repo twice (5.3 MB tarball + 51 MB tree,
# 2043 files). Keep the tarball (it is the verifiable upstream artifact).
FraktalCore/HMI/native/opcua/third_party/mbedtls-*/

# --- PLC: TwinCAT XAE per-machine build + boot output (regenerated on build) ---
FraktalCore/PLC/**/_CompileInfo*/
FraktalCore/PLC/**/_Boot/
FraktalCore/PLC/_Boot/
FraktalCore/PLC/**/*.compileinfo
FraktalCore/PLC/**/_ScopeConfig/
# XAE's "save libraries in project" cache. Dependencies are resolved from the
# version-pinned PlaceholderReference entries; do not publish duplicate Beckhoff
# or older Fraktal compiled libraries from each project.
FraktalCore/PLC/**/_Libraries/
# Generated symbol/export files. TMC generation remains enabled in each PLC
# project for TF6100 commissioning, but the generated output is rebuilt locally.
FraktalCore/PLC/**/*.tmc
FraktalCore/PLC/**/*.tpy
# Compiled library drops belong in signed GitHub Releases, not the source tree.
# Match the ARTEFACTS, not the folder name: an application's `Release/` folder is
# authored source (§4.2 groups a Unit's release engineering under `Release/`), and
# a blanket folder rule silently excluded FB_PressDemoRelease.TcPOU from the repo.
FraktalCore/PLC/**/Release/**/*.library
FraktalCore/PLC/**/Release/*.library
FraktalCore/PLC/**/Release/**/*.compiled-library
FraktalCore/PLC/**/Release/*.compiled-library
# Local dependency/install bundles are machine-bound build inputs, not authored
# Fraktal source. Library versions stay in PlaceholderReference entries.
FraktalCore/PLC/**/Dependancies/
# Local archives and machine-bound TwinCAT trial licensing never leave the PC.
FraktalCore/PLC.7z
FraktalCore/PLC/**/TrialLicense.tclrs
FraktalCore/PLC/**/*.tclrs
*.plcproj.bak
*.tsproj.bak
*.xti.bak
*.dbg.bak
_backup/

# --- Python tooling caches (plc_lint + its fixture suite; regenerated on run) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Reference-only material kept locally, not published ---
NexeedReferenceOnly/
